// Every item that isn't a block (blocks get items from blocks.ron), named
// as in modern Minecraft Java Edition. Runtime item IDs number the block
// items first, then these, in order (see build.rs); saves store names.
//
// Fields (only name and texture are required):
//   texture     name in assets/textures/items/ (without .png). Animated items
//               (compass, clock) use their first frame.
//   max_stack   most per stack, default 64 (1 for tools, armor, buckets...)
//   durability  uses before breaking, for items that aren't tier tools
//               (tools take theirs from the tier, as in 1.0.0)
//   tool        mining tool: kind, tier, and optionally base_speed (speed on
//               blocks it isn't made for, default 1), speeds (per block)
//               and wear (durability lost per block broken, default 1),
//               attack (damage with the item, 1 bare handed), attack_speed
//               (swings a second: 4 bare handed, swords 1.6) and hit_wear
//               (durability lost per hit, default 2; swords 1)
//   places      block placed by right-clicking (seeds, redstone...)
//   food        (hunger, saturation, always_edible): eaten by holding
//               right-click for 32 ticks (1.0.0's ItemFood values)
//   leftover    item left after use (stew eaten → bowl, lava bucket burned → bucket)
//   shoots      ammunition used up by drawing and releasing (bow → arrow)
//   bucket      Empty, or Holds(Water) or Holds(Lava): picks up or pours a
//               fluid source by right-clicking
//
// Values are still 1.0.0's; v1.1 milestones switch them as they reach each
// system.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
[
